6. hostap (wpa_supplicant and hostapd)
--------------------------------------

Source:    https://w1.fi/hostap, as vendored in ESP-IDF 7b9cc1ac
           components/wpa_supplicant/src, and hostapd 2.12
License:   BSD-3-Clause (text below)

Partly ported and modified:

- portable/ieee80211/rsn/src/sae.rs: src/common/sae.c and
  dragonfly.c
- portable/ieee80211/ap/src/sae.rs: src/ap/ieee802_11.c
  (handle_auth_sae, sae_sm_step), src/ap/ap_config.h, src/common/sae.c
- portable/ieee80211/ap/src/pmksa.rs: src/ap/pmksa_cache_auth.c and
  src/ap/wpa_auth.c
- portable/ieee80211/sta/src/pmksa.rs: src/rsn_supp/pmksa_cache.c and
  src/rsn_supp/wpa.c
- portable/ieee80211/sta/src/machine/deferred_eapol.rs: behaviour of
  src/rsn_supp/wpa.c


7. esp-hal
----------

Source:    https://github.com/esp-rs/esp-hal, ld/riscv/hal-defaults.x
Copyright: the esp-rs contributors
License:   MIT OR Apache-2.0

firmware/platform/espressif/linker/runtime/link.x repeats its
PROVIDE(interruptN = DefaultHandler) symbol interface.


Not derived
-----------

Test vectors from IEEE Std 802.11 Annex J, RFC 3394 and the Bluetooth Core
sample data are facts and keep their citations. Linux mac80211 (GPL-2.0) is
cited for behaviour only: portable/ieee80211/rsn/src/ccmp_mpdu.rs and
portable/ieee80211/mac/src/data.rs implement the IEEE 802.11 rules
independently.


